# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# letsfinddomain-skill — environment variables
#
# Recommended for the installed slash skill: set variables in your OS
# environment. `.env` is supported for a local checkout and is gitignored.
# Never commit real values.
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Only the AVAILABILITY provider is required. When Spaceship is configured,
# it is selected first by default. Everything else is optional.
# See references/environment.md for how each value is obtained.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------


# === Availability: pick ONE provider ========================================

# --- Option A: Spaceship (recommended) -------------------------------------
# Batch: 20 domains/request. Free with any Spaceship account.
# Get keys: https://www.spaceship.com/application/api-manager/
SPACESHIP_API_KEY=
SPACESHIP_API_SECRET=

# --- Option B: NameSilo ----------------------------------------------------
# Batch: comma-separated list. Single key, free with any account.
# Get key: https://www.namesilo.com/account/api-manager
# NAMESILO_API_KEY=

# --- Option C: GoDaddy -----------------------------------------------------
# One domain/request. Exact first-year and renewal quote.
# Create a Personal Access Token:
# https://developer.godaddy.com/en/docs/api-users/auth/how-to
# GODADDY_PAT=

# --- Option D: Name.com ----------------------------------------------------
# Up to 50 domains/request. Exact first-year and renewal quote.
# Account Settings -> API Tokens:
# https://www.name.com/account/settings/api
# NAMECOM_USERNAME=
# NAMECOM_API_TOKEN=

# --- Option E: Namecheap ---------------------------------------------------
# Up to 50 domains/request. Requires API access plus one whitelisted IPv4.
# Profile -> Tools -> Business & Dev Tools -> Manage Namecheap API Access:
# https://www.namecheap.com/support/api/intro/
# NAMECHEAP_API_USER=
# NAMECHEAP_USERNAME=
# NAMECHEAP_API_KEY=
# NAMECHEAP_CLIENT_IP=

# --- Option F: Dynadot -----------------------------------------------------
# One domain/request for regular accounts; exact quote when available.
# Account Control Panel -> Tools -> API:
# https://www.dynadot.com/domain/api-commands
# DYNADOT_API_KEY=

# --- Option G: Porkbun -----------------------------------------------------
# One domain/request; requires an API key and secret.
# Account -> API Access:
# https://porkbun.com/account/api
# PORKBUN_API_KEY=
# PORKBUN_SECRET_API_KEY=

# --- Option H: Cloudflare Registrar ---------------------------------------
# Up to 20 domains/request. API access requires account/billing setup.
# API token: Dashboard -> My Profile -> API Tokens.
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/registrar/registrar-api/
# CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=
# CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=

# --- Optional fallback: RDAP (no key, trial use only) ----------------------
# Use only when you do not want to create a registrar account.
# RDAP reports registration records, not guaranteed purchasability, and cannot
# answer every TLD (.io and .co have no RDAP server). The script refuses to
# guess for uncovered TLDs rather than report a false "available".
# See references/providers.md#rdap.
# DOMAIN_FINDER_ALLOW_RDAP=1


# === Pricing (optional) =====================================================

# Porkbun's TLD price list is PUBLIC and needs no credentials — the scripts use
# it by default for reference pricing. Availability still defaults to Spaceship
# whenever SPACESHIP_API_KEY and SPACESHIP_API_SECRET are configured.
#
# Set a different reference registrar only if you buy elsewhere and want its
# prices instead. Supported: porkbun (default) | dynadot | none
# DOMAIN_FINDER_PRICE_SOURCE=porkbun

# Dynadot — also works as an availability provider above. When used only as a
# pricing source, it gives exact per-domain quotes incl. premium pricing, but
# makes ONE request per available domain.
# Get key: https://www.dynadot.com/account/domain/setting/api.html
# DYNADOT_API_KEY=


# === Behaviour defaults (optional) ==========================================
# All of these are suggestions, not enforced rules. Leave unset for no limit.

# Hide candidates whose first-year registration price exceeds this (USD).
# DOMAIN_FINDER_MAX_PRICE=

# Comma-separated TLDs to query when the user does not specify any.
# DOMAIN_FINDER_DEFAULT_TLDS=com

# Seconds to cache price data on disk. Default 86400 (1 day).
# DOMAIN_FINDER_PRICE_TTL=86400


# === Rate limiting (optional) ===============================================
# Request budgets are enforced across separate runs AND parallel processes via
# a lock-guarded state file in .cache/. Full explanation and the reasoning
# behind each default: references/rate-limits.md
#
# Lower these if something else shares the same API key. Raising them past what
# the provider documents just moves the throttling to their servers, where it
# costs you a 429 instead of a short sleep.

# Spaceship documents 30 requests per user per 30s; we default to 25 for headroom.
# DOMAIN_FINDER_SPACESHIP_LIMIT=25
# DOMAIN_FINDER_SPACESHIP_WINDOW=30

# NameSilo does not publish a precise figure. Automated traffic uses /apibatch;
# this default is deliberately low.
# DOMAIN_FINDER_NAMESILO_LIMIT=20
# DOMAIN_FINDER_NAMESILO_WINDOW=60

# GoDaddy's current guide reports a 600-request credential window of about
# 23 minutes and says values can change; the client leaves headroom and reads
# RateLimit-* response headers when present.
# DOMAIN_FINDER_GODADDY_LIMIT=540
# DOMAIN_FINDER_GODADDY_WINDOW=1380
# DOMAIN_FINDER_NAMECOM_LIMIT=20
# DOMAIN_FINDER_NAMECOM_WINDOW=60
# Namecheap documents 50/min, 700/hour, and 8000/day across the whole key.
# DOMAIN_FINDER_NAMECHEAP_LIMIT=45
# DOMAIN_FINDER_NAMECHEAP_WINDOW=60
# Regular Dynadot accounts are 1 thread and 60/min (about 1/sec).
# DOMAIN_FINDER_DYNADOT_LIMIT=55
# DOMAIN_FINDER_DYNADOT_WINDOW=60
# DOMAIN_FINDER_PORKBUN_LIMIT=60
# DOMAIN_FINDER_PORKBUN_WINDOW=60
# Cloudflare's global token limit is 1200/5m; the client leaves room for other calls.
# DOMAIN_FINDER_CLOUDFLARE_LIMIT=180
# DOMAIN_FINDER_CLOUDFLARE_WINDOW=60

# RDAP goes through a shared free public proxy. This is a politeness budget,
# not a published limit. Please don't raise it.
# DOMAIN_FINDER_RDAP_LIMIT=60
# DOMAIN_FINDER_RDAP_WINDOW=60

# Availability result cache, in seconds. Repeated checks of overlapping
# candidate lists then cost zero requests. Set 0 to disable.
# DOMAIN_FINDER_CACHE_TTL=3600
